# shellcheck configuration for AI Dev Autopilot.
#
# Kept in the repository rather than in the CI job so a local `shellcheck bin/*`
# and the CI run answer the same question. Every exclusion below is a whole-repo
# false positive with a reason; anything narrower belongs in a per-line
# `# shellcheck disable=` comment next to the code that needs it, where the
# reason is visible to whoever reads that code.

# SC1007 — "Remove space after = if trying to assign a value".
# Fires on `CDPATH= cd -- ...`, which is the deliberate idiom every entry point
# here uses to resolve its own directory: clearing CDPATH for the duration of one
# `cd` stops a user's CDPATH from silently relocating it. It also fires on
# `local tok val url= saw_url=0`, where the empty initialiser is intentional.
disable=SC1007

# SC2088 — "Tilde does not expand in quotes. Use $HOME".
# Every occurrence is a literal tilde on purpose: a check NAME printed to the
# user ("~/.claude/settings.json matches the hub"), or a test payload that exists
# precisely to assert the guard resolves the `~` spelling itself. Expanding them
# would make the output machine-specific and would delete the thing under test.
# The real bug this rule catches — a tilde in a path a command will act on — is
# covered from the other side by tests/guard-portability.test.sh, which pins path
# resolution through $HOME and $AI_DEV_HOME in both directions.
disable=SC2088
